---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import PageHeader from '@/components/PageHeader.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms"
  description="How to use the Elixir Community directory and newsletter."
>
  <div class="container-page">
    <PageHeader title="Terms" />
    <article class="typography mt-12 max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm text-(--ec-muted)">Updated 7 October 2026</p>
      <p>
        Elixir Community is a directory of Elixir resources, events, jobs and
        people, plus a newsletter. These terms cover how to use it.
      </p>

      <h2>Check before you rely on a listing</h2>
      <p>
        We try to keep everything accurate, but dates, jobs, links and services
        change. Before you book, apply or buy, check with the organiser,
        employer, publisher or service. An older entry does not mean a group,
        podcast or company is still active, or still uses Elixir.
      </p>

      <h2>Names, logos and links</h2>
      <p>
        We use names, logos and images to identify resources and the people who
        make them. They belong to their owners. A listing does not mean they
        endorse us or work with us.
      </p>

      <h2>The newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        The newsletter is free and optional. You join by confirming your email
        and can unsubscribe at any time. The <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a>{' '}
        explains how we handle your email address.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections and removals</h2>
      <p>
        If a listing is wrong, a link is broken, or you have a rights concern,
        email <a href="mailto:hello@elixir.community">hello@elixir.community</a>{' '}
        or open a pull request on the repository linked in the footer. When you
        suggest a listing, please do not include anyone's private information.
      </p>

      <h2>Your legal rights</h2>
      <p>Nothing in these terms takes away rights you have under the law.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
